  "rendered_text": "Jedison\n\n\n  \n\n    Framework-agnostic JavaScript library that generates and validates forms from JSON Schema.\n    \n\n\n    Explore the docs »\n    \n\n\n    \n\n\n    View Playground\n    ·\n    Report Bug\n    ·\n    Request Feature\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\nWhat is Jedison\n\n\nJedison generates forms from JSON schemas. Simply provide a JSON schema and Jedison automatically creates a complete, interactive form with built-in validation.\n\n\nHere's a simple example:\n\n\n{\n  \"title\": \"Contact\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"name\": {\n      \"title\": \"Name\",\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"email\": {\n      \"title\": \"E-Mail\",\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"format\": \"email\",\n      \"minLength\": 3\n    },\n    \"message\": {\n      \"title\": \"Message\",\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"x-format\": \"textarea\"\n    },\n    \"gdpr\": {\n      \"title\": \"I have read and accept the privacy policy\",\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"default\": false,\n      \"const\": true,\n      \"x-format\": \"checkbox\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n\n\nThis schema automatically generates a complete contact form:\n\n\n\n\n\nJedison helps you validate JSON data on the backend and generate interactive forms from JSON Schemas on the frontend.\n\n\nBackend Validation: Jedison can also be used in headless mode for backend validation in Node.js environments. This is optional - you can use any other JSON schema validator you prefer for server-side validation.\n\n\nOne common workflow looks like this:\n\n\n\n\nYour backend sends the JSON Schema to the client\n\n\nJedison automatically renders a complete form based on the schema\n\n\nUsers interact with the form while getting instant client-side validation\n\n\nValidated data gets submitted back to your server\n\n\nThe same schema validates the data again server-side for security (using Jedison in headless mode or any other validator)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBut Jedison is flexible enough to support other patterns too - you might use it for:\n\n\n\n\nStandalone client-side forms without server validation\n\n\nPure server-side JSON validation in your backend services (headless mode)\n\n\nHybrid approaches where different parts of the schema are used in different contexts\n\n\n\n\nMultiple JSON Schema drafts\n\n\nJedison follows draft 2020-12 and also understands schemas written for draft-04, draft-06, draft-07 and 2019-09. Declare the draft with $schema and Jedison normalizes the schema, so the same form and validation work for all of them:\n\n\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"array\",\n  \"items\": [{ \"type\": \"number\" }, { \"type\": \"number\" }],\n  \"additionalItems\": false\n}\n\n\n\nValidation is tested against the official JSON-Schema-Test-Suite for every supported draft. $dynamicRef and $recursiveRef are not supported.\n\n\nComing from JSON Editor?\n\n\nThe JSON Editor README says the library is in maintenance mode and points to Jedison for active development.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJedison\n\n\nJSON Editor\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJSON Schema drafts\n\n\n4, 6, 7, 2019-09, 2020-12\n\n\n3 and 4\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThemes\n\n\nBootstrap 3, 4, 5, Tailwind 4\n\n\nBootstrap 3, 4, 5, Spectre, Tailwind\n\n\n\n\n\n\nStatus\n\n\nActively developed\n\n\nMaintenance mode\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe basic API is close (getValue, setValue, on('change')). See the comparison and migration guide.\n\n\nInstall\n\n\nUsing ES Module\n\n\nnpm\n\n\nnpm install jedison\n\n\n\nyarn\n\n\nyarn add jedison\n\n\n\n<div id=\"jedison-container\"></div>\n\n<script type=\"module\">\n    import Jedison from 'jedison'\n\n    const jedison = new Jedison.Create({\n        container: document.querySelector('#jedison-container'),\n        theme: new Jedison.Theme(),\n        schema: {\n            \"title\": \"Person\",\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n                \"name\": {\n                    \"type\": \"string\",\n                    \"description\": \"The person's  name.\"\n                },\n                \"age\": {\n                    \"description\": \"Age in years which must be equal to or greater than zero.\",\n                    \"type\": \"integer\",\n                    \"minimum\": 0\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    })\n</script>\n\n\n\nUsing fromCDN\n\n\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/jedison@latest/dist/umd/jedison.umd.js\"></script>\n\n<div id=\"jedison-container\"></div>\n\n<script>"
}
